# fashion-hub — Vite/React → Next.js Migration Plan

> Target scaffold:
> `bunx --bun shadcn@latest init --preset b6GfB1vq4 --template next --pointer`
>
> Everything in this document about the preset was **verified by actually running
> the command** into a scratch directory and reading the output — not inferred.
> Baseline scaffold builds clean on Next 16.2.6 / Turbopack.

---

## 0. TL;DR — the three things that will surprise you

1. **The `.` trick does not work.** `--template next` *always* creates a
   subdirectory. Three variants were tested and all fail (§2). The migration must
   scaffold to a temp dir and merge back into `.`.
2. **This is not a "port React Router to App Router" job.** The preset swaps the
   entire substrate: Radix → **Base UI**, lucide → **hugeicons**, Tailwind v3 →
   **v4 (CSS-first, no config file)**, React 18 → **19**, and style `default` →
   **`base-luma`**. Every one of the 49 files in `src/components/ui/` is replaced,
   not edited.
3. **Dark mode arrives switched on.** The preset ships `next-themes` with
   `defaultTheme="system"`. Today's UI is hardcoded light (`bg-white`,
   `text-slate-900`). On a dark-mode machine the migrated app renders broken until
   the colors are tokenized (§5).

---

## 1. Current state (inventory)

| | |
|---|---|
| Build | Vite 5 + `@vitejs/plugin-react-swc` |
| Framework | React 18.3, `react-router-dom` 6.26 |
| Styling | Tailwind **v3.4** + `tailwind.config.ts` + `src/index.css` (HSL vars) |
| Primitives | Radix UI (29 `@radix-ui/*` packages) |
| Icons | `lucide-react` (30 distinct icons in app code) |
| shadcn style | `default`, baseColor `slate`, `rsc: false` |
| Lovable | `lovable-tagger` dev plugin, Lovable OG meta in `index.html` |

**Application code** — 4 pages, 6 components, 1 util:

```
src/pages/Index.tsx          dashboard, grid/list, search+filter, hosts CanvasEditor
src/pages/Profile.tsx        profile form
src/pages/CustomerView.tsx   read-only client view + comments
src/pages/NotFound.tsx       404
src/components/AppSidebar.tsx      CanvasCard.tsx    CanvasEditor.tsx
src/components/ClientInfoPanel.tsx CreateCanvasModal.tsx  ShareModal.tsx
src/utils/pdfExport.ts       window.open + document.write + print()
```

**`src/components/ui/` holds 49 files but app code imports only 8:**
`button` (7×), `input` (6×), `textarea` (5×), `sidebar` (2×), `card`,
`tooltip`, `sonner`, `toaster`.

> **The other 41 UI files are dead code.** Do not migrate them. Re-add from the
> registry on demand.

**Also dead:** `@tanstack/react-query` — `App.tsx` mounts `QueryClientProvider`
but there is not a single `useQuery`/`useMutation` in the codebase. Drop it.

---

## 2. ⚠️ The scaffolding problem — verified

The intent was `... --template next --pointer .` so it lands in the current
folder. **It does not.** All three forms were tested:

| Command | Result |
|---|---|
| `init ... --template next --pointer .` in **this repo** | ✖ `We could not detect a supported framework`. The trailing `.` is parsed as a **component path** (signature is `init [options] [components...]`), which flips the CLI into "add to existing project" mode and ignores `--template`. |
| `init ... --template next --pointer .` in an **empty** dir | Ignores the `.`, prompts *"What is your project named?"*, then creates a **subfolder**. |
| `init ... --name .` | ✖ `dest already exists.` |

**There is no in-place mode.** `--template next` delegates to the Next scaffolder,
which refuses an existing destination.

### The approach that works

```bash
# from repo root, on a migration branch, with a clean tree
bunx --bun shadcn@latest init \
  --preset b6GfB1vq4 --template next --pointer \
  --name .next-scaffold -y

# merge scaffold into repo root, then discard the shell
rsync -a --exclude .git .next-scaffold/ .
rm -rf .next-scaffold
```

`.next-scaffold/` contains its own `git init`; the `--exclude .git` is what stops
it clobbering this repo's history. **Verify `git status` before and after.**

