## 4. 🎨 Colors & fonts the preset brings — full definition

This is the part worth reading closely: the preset is a **gold/amber theme on
neutral greys**, and the current app is **indigo→purple on slate**. They do not
resemble each other.

### Fonts

| Slot | Family | CSS var | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| Sans (body) | **Inter** | `--font-sans` | `next/font/google` |
| Heading | **Inter** | `--font-heading` → aliased to `--font-sans` | same |
| Mono | **Geist Mono** | `--font-mono` | `next/font/google` |

Wired in `app/layout.tsx`; `html { @apply font-sans }` in `globals.css`.
`--font-heading` exists as a distinct token, so headings can be split off later by
pointing it at another family — no component changes needed.

### Color format: **oklch, not HSL**

Current `src/index.css` uses space-separated HSL triplets consumed as
`hsl(var(--primary))`. The preset uses **full `oklch()` values** consumed directly
as `var(--primary)`. Every custom color declaration must be rewritten — a
find/replace of the numbers is not enough, the wrapper function goes away too.

### The palette (light mode, hex computed from the oklch values)

| Token | oklch | ≈ hex | |
|---|---|---|---|
| `--primary` | `0.852 0.199 91.936` | **#fdc700** | gold |
| `--primary-foreground` | `0.421 0.095 57.708` | **#733e0a** | deep amber |
| `--accent` | `0.852 0.199 91.936` | **#fdc700** | same as primary |
| `--secondary` | `0.967 0.001 286.375` | **#f4f4f5** | near-white grey |
| `--destructive` | `0.577 0.245 27.325` | **#e7000b** | red |
| `--background` | `1 0 0` | **#ffffff** | |
| `--foreground` | `0.145 0 0` | near-black | |
| `--sidebar-primary` | `0.681 0.162 75.834` | **#d08700** | darker gold |

Dark mode shifts primary to `oklch(0.795 0.184 86.047)` ≈ **#f0b100**, cards to
`oklch(0.205 0 0)`, and borders to `oklch(1 0 0 / 10%)`.

**Charts** are a five-stop gold ramp (light→dark), not categorical hues:
`#ffdf20 → #f0b100 → #d08700 → ~#a65f00 → #894b00`. If a chart is ever added,
these will not distinguish series well — worth knowing up front.

### Radius & other tokens

`--radius: 0.625rem`, with a **multiplicative** scale that v3 did not have:

```
sm = r*0.6   md = r*0.8   lg = r   xl = r*1.4   2xl = r*1.8   3xl = r*2.2   4xl = r*2.6
```

The `base-luma` Button uses `rounded-4xl` — i.e. **pill-shaped buttons by
default**, a notable visual departure from the current square-ish buttons.

### `--pointer` flag

Adds to `globals.css`:

```css
button:not(:disabled), [role="button"]:not(:disabled) { cursor: pointer; }
```

### Decision taken: **adopt the preset palette fully**

All 140 hardcoded color classes get replaced with semantic tokens:

| Today | Becomes |
|---|---|
| `bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-500 to-purple-600` | `bg-primary text-primary-foreground` |
| `text-slate-500` / `text-slate-600` | `text-muted-foreground` |
| `text-slate-900` | `text-foreground` |
| `bg-white/70` / `bg-white/80` | `bg-card/70` |
| `border-slate-200` / `border-slate-300` | `border-border` |
| `bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 via-white to-blue-50` | `bg-background` |
| `bg-green-50 border-green-200 text-green-800` (saved sections) | keep semantic green, or add `--success` token |
| `bg-blue-50 text-blue-700` (comments) | `bg-muted text-muted-foreground` |
| `bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-700` (status pill) | `bg-primary/15 text-primary` |

Payoff: dark mode works for free, and the app picks up the gold identity.

---

## 5. Tailwind v3 → v4 breakages present in *this* code

Counted against `src/pages` + `src/components/*.tsx`:

| Pattern | Count | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `bg-gradient-to-*` | 14 | → `bg-linear-to-*` (renamed in v4). Most are being deleted anyway per §4. |
| `space-x-*` / `space-y-*` | 45 | v4 changed the selector to `:where(& > :not(:last-child))`. **Visually inspect each** — flex rows with `space-x` are the risky ones. Prefer converting to `gap-*`. |
| bare `border` / `border-t` / `border-b` with no color | 10 | **v4's default border color is `currentColor`, not `gray-200`.** These will render as dark/near-black lines. Must add `border-border` explicitly. |
| `focus:ring-*` | 3 | v4 default ring width changed 3px→1px; `ring` → `ring-3` where the old look is wanted. |
| `shadow-sm` | 2 | v4 renamed the scale: old `shadow-sm` → `shadow-xs`, old `shadow` → `shadow-sm`. |
| `outline-none` | in ui/ | → `outline-hidden`. |

The bare-`border` one is the sneaky one — it is silent, not a build error.

---

## 6. Icons — much cheaper than expected

Discovery: `@hugeicons/core-free-icons` exports **13,556** symbols, and it ships
**lucide-compatible alias names**. All 30 icons this app uses resolve as exact
name matches:

```
Plus Search Filter Grid List Calendar User Palette Bell ArrowLeft Save Share
Upload Type Image Download MessageSquare Home Settings Eye Clock MoreHorizontal
X Copy Mail Link Ruler DollarSign Phone Building          → 30/30 exact
```

So this is a mechanical rewrite, **not** a hand-mapping exercise. The identifiers
stay identical; only the import source and the JSX form change. Note the exports
are **icon data arrays**, not components — hence the `HugeiconsIcon` wrapper:

```tsx
// before
import { Plus, Palette } from 'lucide-react'
<Plus className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />

// after
import { HugeiconsIcon } from '@hugeicons/react'
import { Plus, Palette } from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
<HugeiconsIcon icon={Plus} className="w-4 h-4 mr-2" />
```

`HugeiconsIcon` props: `icon` (required), `size`, `strokeWidth`,
`absoluteStrokeWidth`, `altIcon`/`showAlt`, `primaryColor`/`secondaryColor`, plus
all SVG attributes — so `className` keeps working.

⚠️ Same name ≠ same artwork. Hugeicons' `Save`, for instance, is a different glyph
from lucide's floppy disk. **Do a visual pass after the swap.** If a specific
result is wanted, the `*Icon`-suffixed exports (e.g. `FloppyDiskIcon`,
`PlusSignIcon`) are the native hugeicons names.

---

## 7. Routing map

| Now (react-router) | Next App Router |
|---|---|
| `<Route path="/" element={<Index/>}>` | `app/page.tsx` |
| `/profile` | `app/profile/page.tsx` |
| `/customer-view` | `app/customer-view/page.tsx` |
| `<Route path="*" element={<NotFound/>}>` | `app/not-found.tsx` |
| `BrowserRouter` + `Routes` in `App.tsx` | deleted — `app/layout.tsx` takes over |
| `useLocation()` in NotFound | drop; `not-found.tsx` gets no pathname. Use `usePathname()` in a client child if the log is still wanted |
| `<a href={item.url}>` in AppSidebar | `next/link` `<Link href>` |
| `window.history.back()` in Profile | `useRouter().back()` from `next/navigation` |

**`"use client"` is required** on every one of these — all four pages and all six
components use `useState`/handlers. `rsc: true` in components.json means files are
server components by default. Plan: mark leaf components client, keep
`app/layout.tsx` and `page.tsx` shells as server where possible.

`CanvasEditor` is currently rendered from `Index` via `selectedCanvas` state, not a
route. **Keep it as state for the migration** — promoting it to `/canvas/[id]`
is a behavior change and belongs in a follow-up.

---

## 8. Toasts

`src/components/ui/{toaster,use-toast}.tsx` + `src/hooks/use-toast.ts` are the
**deprecated** Radix toast. Confirmed against the registry:

- `base-luma/toaster` → **404**
- `base-luma/use-toast` → **404**
- `base-luma/sonner` → 200 ✅

So `<Toaster />` in `App.tsx` is dropped and **sonner is the only toast path**.
(Neither is actually invoked anywhere in app code today — no `toast()` calls
exist — so this is pure deletion.)

